12
01:08:00,000 --> 01:08:06,000
Seven Years in Tibet is a 1997 American biographical war
drama film directed by Jean-Jacques Annaud.

13
01:13:40,000 --> 01:13:46,000
It is based on Austrian mountaineer and Schutzstaffel (SS) sergeant Heinrich Harrer's 1952
memoir of the same name, about his experiences in Tibet between 1944 and 1951.

14
01:19:20,000 --> 01:19:26,000
Seven Years in Tibet stars Brad Pitt and David Thewlis, and has music composed
by John Williams with a feature performance by cellist Yo-Yo Ma.

15
01:25:00,000 --> 01:25:06,000
In the film, Harrer (Pitt) and fellow Austrian Peter Aufschnaiter
(Thewlis) are mountaineering in the 1930s India.

16
01:30:40,000 --> 01:30:46,000
When World War II begins in 1939, their German citizenship results in their
imprisonment in a British prisoner-of-war camp in Dehradun in the Himalayas.

17
01:36:20,000 --> 01:36:26,000
In 1944, Harrer and Aufschnaiter escape the prison and cross the border
into Tibet, traversing the treacherous high plateau.

18
01:42:00,000 --> 01:42:06,000
There, after initially being ordered to return to India, they are welcomed at the
holy city of Lhasa and become absorbed into an unfamiliar way of life.

19
01:47:40,000 --> 01:47:46,000
Harrer is introduced to the 14th Dalai Lama, still a
boy, and becomes one of his tutors.

20
01:53:20,000 --> 01:53:26,000
During their time together, Heinrich becomes a close
friend to the young spiritual leader.

21
01:59:00,000 --> 01:59:06,000
Harrer and Aufschnaiter stay in the country until the Battle of Chamdo in 1950.

22
02:04:40,000 --> 02:04:46,000
The film explores themes of himalaya mountain range, buddhism,
buddhist monk, world war ii, prisoner of war.

23
02:10:20,000 --> 02:10:26,000
The tone is emotional.
